    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`) with all tests green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `displayName` on the owner, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, so this gives `OwnerDto` a `displayName` field (and setter) that appears in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Person.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` computed getter `getDisplayName()` returning `lastName + \", \" + firstName`. Placing it on `Person` keeps the formatting logic in the domain entity where the names live (single responsibility, reusable for any person), and `@Transient` keeps it out of JPA persistence.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps by property name, so `OwnerDto.displayName` is populated automatically from `Owner.getDisplayName()` (inherited from `Person`) with no extra mapping code. The reverse `toOwner` mapping is unaffected since it's read-only with no corresponding setter on the entity.",
